{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "39836012",
      "title": "Scoping CSS Rules with CSS Modules",
      "sourceHash": "b851026524cd05cb6103909b58c36eb83f80613471fe040e72ec365ac757ae07",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.81,
          "end": 2.73,
          "en": "So using just CSS",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 2.73,
          "end": 5.355,
          "en": "is definitely not a bad option.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.355,
          "end": 8.67,
          "en": "As you saw, it's pretty easy to separate code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.67,
          "end": 11.94,
          "en": "and to apply styles conditionally",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 11.94,
          "end": 16.11,
          "en": "but we have this one potentially big disadvantage,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 16.11,
          "end": 21.11,
          "en": "that CSS code and CSS rules are not scoped to components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 21.36,
          "end": 24.51,
          "en": "that you can accidentally write CSS code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 24.51,
          "end": 27.483,
          "en": "that affects more components that it should affect.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 28.77,
          "end": 31.41,
          "en": "And we can see this in our application here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 31.41,
          "end": 33.27,
          "en": "when we take a look at these labels,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 33.27,
          "end": 37.625,
          "en": "they are now centered and initially they weren't.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 37.625,
          "end": 41.58,
          "en": "But they are centered because these labels",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 41.58,
          "end": 45.123,
          "en": "are inside of a paragraph, just as the input here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 46.53,
          "end": 49.56,
          "en": "And therefore due to this rule in Header CSS,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 49.56,
          "end": 52.59,
          "en": "which I changed earlier in this section,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 52.59,
          "end": 56.91,
          "en": "where for all paragraphs I align my text in the center,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 56.91,
          "end": 59.79,
          "en": "I also got these centered labels,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 59.79,
          "end": 62.97,
          "en": "which is not the look I wanna have here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 62.97,
          "end": 67.38,
          "en": "Now of course, the fix here is to bring back that header",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 67.38,
          "end": 70.26,
          "en": "in front of the paragraph so that now",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 70.26,
          "end": 74.338,
          "en": "I only target paragraphs that are inside of a header.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 74.338,
          "end": 79.32,
          "en": "But this of course also implies that I as a developer",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 79.32,
          "end": 83.22,
          "en": "am forced to carefully think about my rules",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 83.22,
          "end": 87.24,
          "en": "and my selectors here, which might be a good thing,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 87.24,
          "end": 89.91,
          "en": "but which also means some extra work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 89.91,
          "end": 92.91,
          "en": "It would be nicer if this would instead be scoped.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 92.91,
          "end": 95.91,
          "en": "So if it couldn't affect any other component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 95.91,
          "end": 98.03999999999999,
          "en": "than the component that is defined",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 98.03999999999999,
          "end": 100.68299999999999,
          "en": "in the file where I'm importing this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 102.42,
          "end": 105.36,
          "en": "And that's exactly the behavior you can achieve",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 105.36,
          "end": 110.36,
          "en": "with CSS Modules, which allows you to write Vanilla CSS code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 110.88,
          "end": 114.53999999999999,
          "en": "and rules that are then scoped.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 114.53999999999999,
          "end": 119.53999999999999,
          "en": "Now, CSS Modules is an approach, a solution",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 120.33,
          "end": 124.439,
          "en": "you could say, that in the end needs to be implemented",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 124.439,
          "end": 126.66,
          "en": "and enforced by the build process",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 126.66,
          "end": 129.24,
          "en": "that's used in your React project.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 129.24,
          "end": 133.653,
          "en": "It's not a default browser or JavaScript feature.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 134.55,
          "end": 139.53,
          "en": "Instead, CSS Modules is an approach where the build tool",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 139.53,
          "end": 143.22,
          "en": "will transform your CSS class names",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 143.22,
          "end": 146.34,
          "en": "and only those two class names",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 146.34,
          "end": 150.363,
          "en": "that are guaranteed to be unique per file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 151.26,
          "end": 152.73,
          "en": "And to show you what I mean,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 152.73,
          "end": 156.18,
          "en": "let's switch from the P element selector here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 156.18,
          "end": 160.26,
          "en": "in Header CSS to the let's say paragraph class selector",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 160.26,
          "end": 162.393,
          "en": "with this dot here in front of it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 164.52,
          "end": 167.13,
          "en": "Now of course we can add that here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 167.13,
          "end": 172.13,
          "en": "with class name paragraph, and as a result,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 173.01,
          "end": 176.73,
          "en": "you will see that this still gets the same style as before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 176.73,
          "end": 179.67000000000002,
          "en": "These labels now no longer get those styles",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 179.67000000000002,
          "end": 182.403,
          "en": "because those don't have that class.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 183.33,
          "end": 187.05,
          "en": "But if I would add this class here to this paragraph",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 187.05,
          "end": 189.18,
          "en": "that contains my label",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 189.18,
          "end": 193.86,
          "en": "with class name paragraph, then you would see",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 193.86,
          "end": 195.96,
          "en": "that with this added here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 195.96,
          "end": 199.03300000000002,
          "en": "this is again centered because just by using",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 199.03300000000002,
          "end": 201.24,
          "en": "a CSS class as a selector,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 201.24,
          "end": 203.403,
          "en": "these styles do not get scoped.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 204.87,
          "end": 208.14,
          "en": "But they will now get scoped if you now rename",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 208.14,
          "end": 213.03300000000002,
          "en": "the header CSS file to header.module.CSS.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 215.37,
          "end": 218.85,
          "en": "This .module naming pattern here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 218.85,
          "end": 223.85,
          "en": "is basically a signal for the underlying build process.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 223.98,
          "end": 226.38,
          "en": "So for this Vite build tool,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 226.38,
          "end": 228.9,
          "en": "which is getting used in this project here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 228.9,
          "end": 233.71,
          "en": "to process this file here slightly differently",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 235.56,
          "end": 239.34,
          "en": "because now we also have to import it differently,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 239.34,
          "end": 243.42,
          "en": "not just because we must change this name of course",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 243.42,
          "end": 247.11,
          "en": "But also because now we must import something",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 247.11,
          "end": 250.23,
          "en": "from this header.module file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 250.23,
          "end": 253.59,
          "en": "and that something will be a JavaScript object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 253.59,
          "end": 257.283,
          "en": "that will be generated by that underlying build process,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 258.12,
          "end": 261.089,
          "en": "which you could name classes or styles,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 261.089,
          "end": 262.57,
          "en": "whatever you want",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 263.58,
          "end": 265.63,
          "en": "But classes is a fitting name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 266.721,
          "end": 267.554,
          "en": "because this object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 267.554,
          "end": 270.24,
          "en": "will contain your class names",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 270.24,
          "end": 273.003,
          "en": "transformed to unique class names.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 274.23,
          "end": 276.813,
          "en": "For example, here for this paragraph class.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 278.13,
          "end": 280.29,
          "en": "Now with this import added,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 280.29,
          "end": 282.9,
          "en": "we can go to this paragraph",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 282.9,
          "end": 285.81,
          "en": "and instead of adding paragraph as a text value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 285.81,
          "end": 290.7,
          "en": "for class name, we should now add a dynamic value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 290.7,
          "end": 295.15,
          "en": "and use this class's object that we are importing up here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 296.90999999999997,
          "end": 301.87,
          "en": "to access .paragraph here, .paragraph because I have",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 304.77,
          "end": 307.65,
          "en": "a class named paragraph in there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 307.65,
          "end": 309.72,
          "en": "If this would be named para,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 309.72,
          "end": 314.72,
          "en": "we would have to access .para here, but I chose paragraph",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 315.48,
          "end": 318.513,
          "en": "as a name, so I'll use that in both files.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 320.91,
          "end": 322.92,
          "en": "With that, if you save that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 322.92,
          "end": 326.1,
          "en": "you'll see the same result as before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 326.1,
          "end": 328.35,
          "en": "But if you inspect this paragraph",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 328.35,
          "end": 331.953,
          "en": "In the header now. you'll see something interesting there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 333.84000000000003,
          "end": 337.714,
          "en": "If you take a look at the class that's actually applied",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 337.714,
          "end": 338.55,
          "en": "In the rendered DOM,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 338.55,
          "end": 341.505,
          "en": "you see that it has this weird name here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 341.505,
          "end": 345.24,
          "en": "which is definitely not the name we chose.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 345.24,
          "end": 348.34000000000003,
          "en": "It includes paragraph, but it also then",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 349.21,
          "end": 350.96,
          "en": "includes more characters and words.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 352.2,
          "end": 355.71,
          "en": "And this strange class name here was in the end",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 355.71,
          "end": 359.43,
          "en": "generated by the built build tool automatically.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 359.43,
          "end": 361.86,
          "en": "And if you take a look at the head section here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 361.86,
          "end": 366.567,
          "en": "you'll see that in the injected style here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 366.567,
          "end": 369.24,
          "en": "we got all the other element selectors",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 369.24,
          "end": 370.71,
          "en": "we got before as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 370.71,
          "end": 374.07,
          "en": "But this paragraph class here was transformed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 374.07,
          "end": 375.99,
          "en": "The name of it was transformed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 375.99,
          "end": 378.93,
          "en": "It is that weird name we saw being applied",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 378.93,
          "end": 381.483,
          "en": "to that paragraph a couple of seconds ago.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 383.46,
          "end": 386.4,
          "en": "And that's the idea behind CSS modules.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 386.4,
          "end": 390.9,
          "en": "This class name is now unique for this component file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 390.9,
          "end": 395.9,
          "en": "and therefore for this component, if I add paragraph",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 396.15,
          "end": 401.15,
          "en": "as a text here in another file, in another component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 401.61,
          "end": 406.17,
          "en": "you'll see that this label is not affected by it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 406.17,
          "end": 411.17,
          "en": "Indeed, if I inspect this control here and this paragraph,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 411.39,
          "end": 413.972,
          "en": "it does have this paragraph class of course",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 413.972,
          "end": 415.74,
          "en": "but this has no effect",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 415.74,
          "end": 418.32,
          "en": "because this original paragraph class name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 418.32,
          "end": 422.07,
          "en": "I defined in the header.module CSS file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 422.07,
          "end": 424.95,
          "en": "get transformed by that build process,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 424.95,
          "end": 427.26,
          "en": "and therefore this build process in the end",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 427.26,
          "end": 431.67,
          "en": "ensures that my class styles are scoped",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 431.67,
          "end": 434.193,
          "en": "to the component file in which I'm importing them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 435.33,
          "end": 439.29,
          "en": "And that's how you can achieve CSS rule scoping",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 439.29,
          "end": 441.873,
          "en": "with almost Vanilla CSS.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 443.4,
          "end": 445.92,
          "en": "And of course, you could now also apply a class",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 445.92,
          "end": 448.62,
          "en": "like this conditionally if you wanted to.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 448.62,
          "end": 450.3,
          "en": "If you had some condition here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 450.3,
          "end": 452.90999999999997,
          "en": "and that's of course now just a dummy example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 452.90999999999997,
          "end": 457.26,
          "en": "you could apply either this class or no class,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 457.26,
          "end": 460.8,
          "en": "depending on whether this condition here is met or not.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 460.8,
          "end": 463.59000000000003,
          "en": "So you can still apply this conditionally",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 463.59000000000003,
          "end": 466.86,
          "en": "as you learned it before, and you can also inject it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 466.86,
          "end": 471.86,
          "en": "into strings with those here with this syntax here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 472.53,
          "end": 474.63,
          "en": "because of course in the end, the value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 474.63,
          "end": 478.81600000000003,
          "en": "stored under this paragraph property will be a string.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 135,
          "start": 478.81600000000003,
          "end": 482.07,
          "en": "It will be that unique class name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 136,
          "start": 482.07,
          "end": 484.803,
          "en": "that was generated by the build tool.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 137,
          "start": 485.88,
          "end": 487.83,
          "en": "So that all works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 138,
          "start": 487.83,
          "end": 490.35,
          "en": "As you see, if I reload here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 139,
          "start": 490.35,
          "end": 493.5,
          "en": "and therefore it works almost like Vanilla CSS",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 140,
          "start": 493.5,
          "end": 495.363,
          "en": "but you got that extra scoping.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 141,
          "start": 496.86,
          "end": 500.76,
          "en": "Hence for CSS modules, the advantage of course",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 142,
          "start": 500.76,
          "end": 503.67,
          "en": "still is that your CSS code is decoupled",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 143,
          "start": 503.67,
          "end": 507.84,
          "en": "from your JSX code, that you write CSS code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 144,
          "start": 507.84,
          "end": 510.39,
          "en": "as you know and maybe love it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 145,
          "start": 510.39,
          "end": 512.7,
          "en": "that it can be written by another person.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 146,
          "start": 512.7,
          "end": 515.91,
          "en": "So just as we had it for Vanilla CSS,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 147,
          "start": 515.91,
          "end": 519.33,
          "en": "but we now also got the additional advantage",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 148,
          "start": 519.33,
          "end": 521.43,
          "en": "that CSS classes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 149,
          "start": 521.43,
          "end": 525.06,
          "en": "so rules that are using CSS classes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 150,
          "start": 525.06,
          "end": 527.52,
          "en": "are scoped to the component file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 151,
          "start": 527.52,
          "end": 531.363,
          "en": "which imports the CSS file with those rules.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 152,
          "start": 533.46,
          "end": 536.46,
          "en": "Of course, we also still have some disadvantages though",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 153,
          "start": 536.46,
          "end": 539.43,
          "en": "because you still need to know CSS",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 154,
          "start": 539.43,
          "end": 542.418,
          "en": "because we're still writing Vanilla CSS in the end.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 155,
          "start": 542.418,
          "end": 547.23,
          "en": "And a new disadvantage when using CSS Modules",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 156,
          "start": 547.23,
          "end": 548.82,
          "en": "is that you may end up",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 157,
          "start": 548.82,
          "end": 552.9,
          "en": "with many relatively small CSS files",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 158,
          "start": 552.9,
          "end": 556.53,
          "en": "in your project when using CSS Modules",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 159,
          "start": 556.53,
          "end": 558.48,
          "en": "because as you can already see here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 160,
          "start": 558.48,
          "end": 560.61,
          "en": "we got this header module CSS file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 161,
          "start": 560.61,
          "end": 563.76,
          "en": "which contains some CSS code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 162,
          "start": 563.76,
          "end": 567.39,
          "en": "and we could now also add one for auth inputs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 163,
          "start": 567.39,
          "end": 571.02,
          "en": "And if we had a bigger project with more components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 164,
          "start": 571.02,
          "end": 575.22,
          "en": "and every component has its own CSS file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 165,
          "start": 575.22,
          "end": 579.63,
